            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A computer-implemented method for providing gaming assistance, comprising receiving over a network information related to a plurality of game plays of players for a gaming application, determining, from the information, a current game context of a first game play of a first player, wherein the current game context includes game state data that allows for generation of a gaming environment at a current time, determining, from the information, a plurality of historical expert game contexts of a plurality of expert game plays of experts that have played the gaming application, the expert game plays generated from players classified as experts for the gaming application, wherein each of the experts is associated with a plurality of game contexts, each corresponding to a different timestamp, for the gaming application, receiving an assistance query related to the first game play, comparing the current game context of the first player to the plurality of historical expert game contexts to determine at least one historical expert game context that matches the current game context, determining one or more recorded help sessions having the historical expert game contexts that match the current game context, and streaming, to a device of the first player, the one or more recorded help sessions to render assistance to the first player.</p>
